561 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (In their low build-up phase, Leverkusen employs an asymmetrical 1-4-2-3-1 formation, where the left-back, Grimaldo, drops deeper to form a defensive line of four. This structure, along with the goalkeeper and the double pivot in midfield, gives them a numerical advantage, typically seven players, allowing them to break through the press more effectively. The asymmetry is purposeful, as it forces the team to favor the right side for progression, particularly to exploit the speed and offensive capabilities of their right wing-back, Jeremy Frimpong.)
/E (In their low build-up phase, Leverkusen employs an asymmetrical 1-4-2-3-1 formation, where the left-back, Grimaldo, drops deeper to form a defensive line of four. This structure, along with the goalkeeper and the double pivot in midfield, gives them a numerical advantage, typically seven players, allowing them to break through the press more effectively. The asymmetry is purposeful, as it forces the team to favor the right side for progression, particularly to exploit the speed and offensive capabilities of their right wing-back, Jeremy Frimpong.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
562 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Frimpong's presence on the right side obliges the opposing defense to shift more players to that flank, concentrating their efforts to close down Leverkusen's attacking movements. However, this leaves the left side, where Grimaldo operates, more exposed. Grimaldo, who is reliable on the ball and adept at long switches of play, can exploit this with large, diagonal passes that switch the point of attack, catching the opposition off guard and opening up new avenues for Leverkusen's offense.)
/E (Frimpong's presence on the right side obliges the opposing defense to shift more players to that flank, concentrating their efforts to close down Leverkusen's attacking movements. However, this leaves the left side, where Grimaldo operates, more exposed. Grimaldo, who is reliable on the ball and adept at long switches of play, can exploit this with large, diagonal passes that switch the point of attack, catching the opposition off guard and opening up new avenues for Leverkusen's offense.)
