/E (Central Overloads with Wide Isolation: The primary strategy involves overloading the central areas to progress through vertical passing and intricate combinations. By pushing their center-backs high up the pitch, Leverkusen creates numerical superiority in the middle, allowing midfielders like Granit Xhaka and Florian Wirtz to dictate play. The wing-backs, Grimaldo and Frimpong, stay wide to stretch the opposition and create isolation situations on the flanks. This overload in the center often forces the opposition to collapse inward, which then opens space on the wings.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [2]
